# Reference grammar: tutorials/regression/lib.sh.
# probe <file> <time> <column> <expected> <tolerance>
# Values from solids4foam ed7f957f, whose electroMechanicalLaw pushes the active
# stress forward with the deformation gradient (#393).
# Column indices count the whitespace-separated fields of the probe file after
# stripping the parentheses that vector probes write, so time is column 1,
# probe 0 is columns 2..4 for a vector and column 2 for a scalar. Probe 0 is
# at the apex, inside the stimulus region; probe 1 is mid-wall.
#
# The apex activates at 3.2 ms; the mid-wall probe has not activated by 10 ms.
probe  postProcessing/CaiProbes/electro/0/activationTime  0.01   2  0.00323067    1e-5
probe  postProcessing/CaiProbes/electro/0/activationTime  0.01   3  -1            1e-9
# D: apex x and z, mid-wall y, at 5 and 10 ms.
probe  postProcessing/Taprobes/solid/0/D                  0.005  2  2.92255e-05   1e-6
probe  postProcessing/Taprobes/solid/0/D                  0.005  4  -3.44283e-05  1e-6
probe  postProcessing/Taprobes/solid/0/D                  0.005  6  -9.71048e-05  2e-6
probe  postProcessing/Taprobes/solid/0/D                  0.01   2  3.69729e-05   1e-6
probe  postProcessing/Taprobes/solid/0/D                  0.01   4  -4.66866e-05  1e-6
probe  postProcessing/Taprobes/solid/0/D                  0.01   6  -0.000181704  2e-6
# Apical active tension, rising after activation (by 91 Pa from 5 to 10 ms;
# the old 20 ms reference reproduced to all six digits on this build).
probe  postProcessing/Taprobes/solid/0/Ta                 0.005  2  4934.58       10.0
probe  postProcessing/Taprobes/solid/0/Ta                 0.01   2  5025.31       10.0
